  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nThe main southern stream sinusoidal H500 pattern should continue\nthroughout the remainder of the long term forecast period. This\nwill result in additional rain chances going through early next\nweek. Another low pressure system, as of the latest 30/12Z model\nand numerical data should move east over the Panhandles. Rain\nchances will return Sunday night through Tuesday, with some\npotentially strong wind gusts in the wake of the main system and\nits cold front that will move through the region. Higher probs\n(20-50%) favor wind gusts at or over 50 mph mainly for the\nnorthern Panhandles on Monday and Tuesday, and will watch trends\nclosely. Temperatures will be near average for early November for\nSunday and Monday, before dropping off to below average Tuesday\nthrough Thursday of next week.",
